   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "statement",
      "label": "\\( R = 2 \\sqrt{2} \\)"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "For the ratio test, form \\( \\left|\\frac{a_{n+1}}{a_n}\\right| \\) from consecutive terms of \\( \\frac{4 \\left(x - 2\\right)^{2n}}{8^{n} n} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99042",
         "rule_named": "ratio of consecutive terms"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Its limit is \\( \\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\left(\\frac{n}{n+1}\\right) \\frac{\\left|x - 2\\right|^{2}}{8} = \\frac{\\left|x - 2\\right|^{2}}{8} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99043",
         "rule_named": "limit of the ratio"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The series converges when this limit is less than 1: \\( \\left|x - 2\\right|^{2} < 8 \\), that is \\( \\left|x - 2\\right| < 2 \\sqrt{2} \\), so the radius of convergence is \\( R = 2 \\sqrt{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            [
               "Sqrt",
               2
            ]
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99047",
         "rule_named": "radius stated"
